# XCU write
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# The recipient's terminal cannot be used by a test, so only the refusal for a
# user who is not logged on is exercised. The name used is one that no login
# can hold.

assertion  XCU.write.001
anchor     utilities/write.html#EXIT STATUS
class      required
says       write to a user who is not logged on exits with a status above zero.
test       t/001-not-logged-on.sh

assertion  XCU.write.002
anchor     utilities/write.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     utilities/write.html#STDIN
anchor     utilities/write.html#EXIT STATUS
class      untestable
says       write copies lines from standard input to the terminal of a user
           who is logged in, after the header line, ending a session with the
           end-of-text message.
reason     It needs another login with a terminal that the test may write to,
           and the output goes to that terminal and not to the test.
